.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
The first or last row
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Fold or unfold a section; \(-> on a directory or a file of tables goes inside it
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
What the control bar says on this row: "Open all" reads a whole directory as one table, "Inside" steps into it, "Open" loads a file, "Look" finds out first. A place a collection suggests, indented under its dataset, opens whole. On a section header, fold or unfold it; on the More row, show the rest; on the hidden-files row, show them
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
While the filter is empty: fold or unfold the section header under the cursor. With a filter typed, it types
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR
Delete a filter character; on an empty filter, up a level (from a bucket, back to its cloud source; from the top of a collection's remote dataset, back here)
.TP
\fBTab\fR
Cycle the sort; the control bar names the order in effect when it has room
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back out one layer: the path prompt, the filter, the directory (back to the row it was entered from), then to the open table, which the control bar's chip names
.TP
\fBClick\fR
Select the row; double-click is Enter
.TP
\fBWheel\fR
Move the selection three rows, stopping at the ends
.PP
\fIFinding\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow by name or column; fuzzy, so "sal" finds "sales". What you open often ranks first. Typing also searches below the directory you are inside and the listed bucket names; matches appear under "Found"
.TP
\fB~\fR
While the filter is empty: type a path or URL by hand. The list shows the directory being typed, narrowed by the name after the last /. The prompt is a plain editor: characters, Backspace, Ctrl+U clears, Tab completes the one name left or what the names share, \(ua / \(da pick a name, Enter opens a file or goes inside a directory, Esc closes. s3://, gs:// and az:// complete from buckets and prefixes already known. With a filter typed, ~ types into it
.TP
\fBCtrl+U\fR
Clear the filter or path input
.TP
\fBCtrl+R\fR
List again what is on screen
.TP
\fBCtrl+A\fR
Show or hide files datui cannot read; inside a SQLite database, its internal tables
.TP
\fBCtrl+X\fR
Show the local file under the cursor as bytes, in the hex view, whatever datui would read it as
.TP
\fBCtrl+D\fR
Remember the directory under the cursor, so it stays listed; again to forget it. A file stands for the directory it is in, a heading for the one it lists
.TP
\fBDelete\fR
Forget the highlighted recent entry, or a whole place after confirming, or a remembered place on its heading, or hide a cloud source
.TP
\fBShift+Delete\fR
Forget every recent entry, after confirming
.PP
