\fIColumns tab\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow the column list, when the find field is focused
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Cycle the column's sort: none \(-> ascending \(-> descending (each column carries its own direction)
.TP
\fB1\-9\fR
Put the column at that place in the sort order; 0 removes it (a digit past the end of the order says so)
.TP
\fBDel\fR
Remove the column from the sort
.TP
\fB[ / ]\fR
Move the column earlier or later in the sort order
.TP
\fB+ / \- (= / _)\fR
Move the column's display position
.TP
\fBL\fR
Freeze this column and every column up to it at the left edge; on a column already frozen, pull the boundary back
.TP
\fBv\fR
Show or hide the column (it keeps its place, dimmed)
.TP
\fB< / > (, / .)\fR
Make the column 4 cells narrower or wider. A number column is never narrower than its numbers
.TP
\fBf\fR
Fit the column to the rows on screen, its name up to the automatic limit
.TP
\fBw\fR
Back to the automatic width
.TP
\fBC\fR
Clear the staged sort, order, locks, hidden columns and widths
.PP
\fIFilters tab\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Edit the row under the cursor, or add one on the last row. Editing walks three steps on the row: pick the column (type to narrow, Enter chooses), pick the operator the same way, then type the value and Enter saves the row. Tab, \(-> and Space also choose at the column and operator steps; Shift+Tab steps back. \(ua\(da (j/k) move in both lists, and \(da jumps from the find field into the list. Esc backs out of the edit and only the edit.
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Toggle and/or on the row
.TP
\fBd / Del\fR
Delete the row
.TP
\fBC\fR
Clear every staged filter
.TP
Date
2024-01-01
.TP
Date and time
2024-01-01, 2024-01-01 05:30, 2024-01-01T05:30:00.25, a clock in the column's zone; +01:00 or Z names an instant
.TP
Time
05:30, 05:30:00.25
.TP
Duration
1d 2h 30m, 90s, 1500ms (d h m s ms us ns)
.TP
Decimal
1.5, at the column's scale
