.SS "Chart"
\fBc\fR at the table.
.TP
\fB1\-6\fR
Switch chart type directly ([ / ] cycle)
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between the option rows (\(ua/\(da too)
.TP
\fBEnter / Space\fR
Open a column row's picker, toggle an option, or cycle the plot style, range or order
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Cycle the plot style, range or order; adjust bins, bandwidth, or Sample size (+ / \- too)
.TP
\fBPgUp/PgDn\fR
Adjust Sample size in bigger steps
.TP
Sample size
Rows a chart reads. A larger table is sampled across all of it, and the chart says so below the plot
.TP
Range
Histogram, Box Plot and KDE: all values, or p1-p99 (the 1st to 99th percentile); the chart counts the values left out
.TP
Bar
One bar per category: a text, categorical, boolean or integer column. Count counts the rows per category, exactly, over the whole view; a numeric value takes one row per category (group first with a query). Order by value or label; bars that do not fit are counted
.TP
\fBg\fR
Grid on or off at the labeled ticks: XY, Histogram, Box Plot and KDE. [analysis] chart_grid sets where it starts
.TP
\fBx\fR
XY: the plot takes the keys, and a crosshair reads out x and every series' value under the plot. \(<- / \(-> (h/l) step to the next point or column, Home/End go to the ends; x, Tab or Esc hand the keys back to the option rows. A click on the plot puts the crosshair there
.TP
\fBe\fR
Export the chart to PNG or EPS. Needs the chart's required columns picked first
.TP
\fBt\fR
While following a file, draw again with the rows that arrived since; the bar says how many
.TP
\fB? / F1\fR
Show this help (with a picker open ? types into the filter; F1 still opens help)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the table
